{
  "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
  "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:17 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0000-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of United States, as amicus curae, supporting Petitioners."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "John R. Kroger",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In Pearson v. Callahan, this Court gave the lower Federal courts discretionary power to decide substantive questions of constitutional law in qualified immunity cases in order to further the development of constitutional precedent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What -- what is the interest of the -- of the parties who were victorious here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Leondra R. Kruger",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A number of the questions this morning have focused on the question whether a live case or controversy remains because Respondent has chosen not to challenge the Ninth Circuit's qualified immunity ruling and so purportedly has no continuing stake in the resolution of this controversy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But that wouldn't be the case if the opinion were vacated -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Kruger",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It establishes the law such that qualified immunity will not be available in the next case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It would be a partial vacatur, right? The Court's done that before, hasn't it, where we vacate part of a decision under Munsingwear?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0001-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It seems to me it would affect Camreta's behavior and that of other child protective officers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why? What's the test? Isn't the test clearly established law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Kubitschek",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is no case or controversy between S.G. and the Petitioners. That ended when -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Where are you reading in the holding of the court of appeals? Because I was under the impression that they did say there's only three ways: One is you get a warrant; another is you get parental consent; and a third is exigent circumstances."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Kubitschek",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0001-0008",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There was a seizure."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: If the information elicited from the child is that she has been abused by her father, then there is a likelihood that there will be police interest in that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. KUBITSCHEK: No, it would not be the same if it was the school nurse or Mr. Camreta. And the -- the reason is that the school nurse is part of the school administration, and the school has an obligation and the authority under T.L.O. act and in Earls to make rules and carry out procedures that will protect the children of the school and promote learning, and if the child comes -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: But what is your answer to Justice Ginsburg's question, suppose it was just Mr. Camreta or suppose it was the school nurse, would the answer be the same?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. KUBITSCHEK: Well, Your Honor, because child welfare investigations are also harmful to children. And when -- when a child is asked, interrogated about whether or not her father touches her inappropriately, that's not a neutral action. Whether or not she has been abused that causes trauma to the child -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. KUBITSCHEK: The Monell action against the municipality was dismissed on the facts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: General, just a point of clarification before you go on. You said earlier that your office had advised the county not to seize children. Does that mean they're not talking to children at all? Is -- you used the word seized. Are you advising them that they don't have the right to talk to children? Without their parental consent or a warrant?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KROGER: No, Your Honor, we believe that reasonable suspicion is the -- is the proper basis before making a seizure of a child to conduct one of these inquiries."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0002-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KROGER: Yes, Your Honor. That's part of the reason we agreed that a seizure was committed here, so that law enforcement are not placed in a difficult position every time they speak to a child, of trying to make their own determination as to whether -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Ms. Kubitschek said it was based on different events. Is that right or not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: The Fourth Amendment claim against the county is based on -- on this interview?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kroger",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KROGER: Your Honor, I have not seen the new complaint, but my understanding is that it is the same event and same claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "592d5115c17010b8d881eee95e0134b39c04c2d30318b6cddfba30c7d335e308",
      "evidence_id": "ev-592d5115c170-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2010-09-1454",
      "confidence": 0.0,
